-- title:
--   Ordered trees with finite levels
-- statement:
--   These notions belong to a proof that every reflexive real Banach space has the fixed point property for nonexpansive maps: every $F:C\to C$ with $\|Fa-Fb\|\le\|a-b\|$ on a nonempty closed bounded convex set $C$ has a fixed point. The proof assumes a fixed-point-free map, reduces to a minimal invariant set $K$ of diameter $1$, builds an adaptive weighted tree of nonexpansive maps generated by resolvents, and contradicts the minimality through detecting functionals.
--
--   1. **Ordered tree.** Level sizes $s_k\ge1$ with $s_0=1$, and parent maps $\{0..s_{k+1}-1\}\to\{0..s_k-1\}$ that are monotone and surjective. So every node has children, and children of consecutive parents form consecutive blocks.
--   2. **Nodes and root.** Nodes of level $k$ are the indices below $s_k$, and the root is the single node of level $0$.
--   3. **Ancestors and descendants.** For $i\le j$, the ancestor map is the composite of parent maps from level $j$ down to level $i$. The descendants of $v$ at level $j$ are
--   $$
--   \{s:\ \mathrm{anc}_{i,j}(s)=v\}.
--   $$
